    "title": "Additive and ring structure on the sheared colimit of Witt vectors",
    "description": "Model a filtered colimit of rings as a directed union of a monotone family of subrings S : ι → Subring R with colimit ⨆ i, S i. It is known set-theoretically that the finitely-supported (sheared) Witt vectors over the colimit are the union of the images of the functorial maps WittVector.map (S i).subtype over the stages. Upgrade this from a set-level statement to an algebraic one: show that this union is closed under Witt addition and Witt multiplication, hence is a subring of WittVector p (⨆ i, S i), and that the natural map from the ring colimit of the diagram i ↦ image(WittVector.map (S i).subtype) to it is a ring isomorphism. The proposed approach is to exploit that the n-th Witt addition and multiplication polynomials depend only on the first n coordinates (finite arity), so that on finitely-supported vectors both operations preserve finite support and factor through a single stage after merging finitely many indices via directedness.",
    "tags": ["WittVectors", "CommutativeAlgebra", "FilteredColimits"]
  },
