    "description": "For a monotone family of subrings S : ι → Subring R with colimit ⨆ i, S i, consider Mathlib's Frobenius WittVector.frobenius and Verschiebung WittVector.verschiebung endomorphisms of WittVector p R. Conjecture: on finitely-supported Witt vectors, both operators send the union of the stage-images WittVector.map (S i).subtype into itself and are computed stagewise, so that the sheared colimit is a module over the Frobenius/Verschiebung algebra and the isomorphism with the filtered colimit is equivariant. The proposed approach is to combine the coefficient formulas frobenius_coeff / verschiebung_coeff (each output coordinate is a polynomial in finitely many input coordinates, and Verschiebung shifts support by one) with the directed-union merge lemma to show finite support and single-stage factorization are preserved.",
